{
  "borough": "Waltham Forest",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed steel boundary treatment by reason of its\r\ndesign, height and position would represent an unduly dominant and unwelcoming presence\r\nwithin the streetscene, whilst also having a detrimental impact on local\r\nbiodiversity contrary to Policy(s) 53, 77, 79 and 80 of the adopted Waltham\r\nForest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "Notwithstanding the first point of refusal, in the absence\r\nof a BNG Statement/ Draft Biodiversity Gain Plan the applicant has failed to demonstrate\r\nat least a 10% increase in biodiversity value relative to the pre-development\r\nbiodiversity value of the onsite habitat in accordance with Schedule 7A of the\r\nTown and Country Planning Act 1990 (as inserted by Schedule 14 of the\r\nEnvironment Act 2021).",
    "Notwithstanding the first point of refusal, in the absence\r\nof a Tree Survey and Arboricultural Impact Assessment the applicant has failed\r\nto demonstrate that the proposed boundary treatment could be installed without undue\r\nnegative impacts to the existing trees on the boundary. As such, the proposal\r\nwould be contrary to Policy 80 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1\r\n(2024)."
  ],
